(463, 'Skyline 2026: The Edge of Tomorrow', 17, 'Standing above Ho Chi Minh City, where the streets below shape the future — a vertigo-filled fisheye moment captured at the edge of 2026.\r\n📝 Step-by-Step Guide:\r\n1️⃣ Open 👉 Google Gemini\r\n2️⃣ Upload your reference photo 📷 \r\n3️⃣ Copy & paste this prompt ⬇️', 'A fisheye ultra-wide shot looking straight down from an extremely tall skyscraper in Ho Chi Minh City. A smiling young man wearing a black overshirt and a gold chain takes a selfie using a long selfie stick while standing on a circular, transparent glass viewing platform. The shot uses a dramatic ultra-wide fisheye lens, creating strong distortion and an intense sense of height and vertigo.\r\nFar below, Ho Chi Minh City’s urban layout is intentionally designed so that streets, rooftops, buildings, and neighbourhood blocks form the giant numbers “2026” when viewed from above. The city grid curves organically into the digits, blending realistic Vietnamese architecture with a creative, intentional city-wide design. Recognisable HCMC elements such as dense low-rise housing, wider boulevards, greenery, and river-adjacent development subtly reinforce the location.\r\nWarm evening sunlight washes across rooftops, roads, and parks, creating soft highlights and long shadows that give the “2026” numbers a glowing outline. The atmosphere feels cinematic and hyper-realistic, with razor-sharp detail, natural lighting, and a strong sense of scale, danger, and height.\r\nUse the reference image with a 100% face match. Do not stylise, beautify, or alter facial features in any way. Preserve exact likeness, proportions, and skin tone.\r\nAdd a subtle “PicPose” seal/logo at the bottom-left corner, with professional padding to ensure branding is visible but not distracting.', 'uploads/ai_posts_pic/1766050189_2de631736560.png', NULL, '[\"PicPose\",\"Skyline2026\",\"FutureFromAbove\",\"FisheyePhotography\",\"GlassPlatform\",\"UrbanIllusion\",\"HoChiMinhCity\",\"CityFromSky\",\